Patch: make the sing-box sidecar usable on Android
=====================================================

Why this is needed
-------------------
internal/subs/singbox.go decides the release asset from runtime.GOOS/GOARCH:

    func singBoxPlatform() (string, string) { return runtime.GOOS, runtime.GOARCH }
    // suffix: "-<goos>-<goarch>.tar.gz"

On an Android build GOOS is "android", so it asks SagerNet for
"sing-box-<ver>-android-arm64.tar.gz" — an asset that does not exist, and the
sidecar never starts. Android userland is Linux, so the right asset is
"-linux-arm64.tar.gz". One function is the whole fix.

Apply from the goroot checkout root:

    patch -p1 < ../patches/subs-android.patch

or just edit the single line by hand (see below) — the patch is 1 line.

--- a/internal/subs/singbox.go
+++ b/internal/subs/singbox.go
@@ -38,7 +38,17 @@
 // singBoxPlatform is the pair this build asks for.
-func singBoxPlatform() (string, string) { return runtime.GOOS, runtime.GOARCH }
+func singBoxPlatform() (string, string) {
+	goos, goarch := runtime.GOOS, runtime.GOARCH
+	// Android has no sing-box release of its own; its userland is the Linux
+	// one. Without this the sidecar asks for an asset that does not exist and
+	// the whole rotation feature silently degrades to direct dialing.
+	if goos == "android" {
+		goos = "linux"
+	}
+	return goos, goarch
+}
